{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"title":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:bufferDropReporter:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidBatchBufferLimit","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"],"title":"Delivering","anchor":"Delivering"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where tracked events go: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is a plain sink with one requirement, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which is given","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch of records, oldest first. Delivering is a chain of operators over a tracker’s records:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"text":" gathers them into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds while any are pending, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"text":" hands each batch to every destination as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lazy unit of work that runs once you call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slow one delays only itself. A full buffer drops its oldest batch and reports it as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport","type":"reference"},{"text":". When the tracker has a store, the delivery reads the dropped batch’s records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"back for that destination once it catches up, and tells the store when each batch has reached","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every destination.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","isActive":true},{"text":", and added to by ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)","isActive":true},{"text":", which runs an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher","isActive":true},{"text":" on the records that destination alone receives. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints each event, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","isActive":true},{"text":" keeps the newest records it receives for the app to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read, in a debug view or a test.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logs, traces and servers have destinations in modules of their own, so an app links only the ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it uses: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggerDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggingDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpanEventDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TracingDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct Uploader: Destination {","    func receive(_ batch: [EventRecord]) async {","        \/\/ Send the batch, and return once it is somewhere it won't be lost.","    }","}","","let inspector = try InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(","        to: Uploader().accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite(),","        inspector","    )","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let received = inspector.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The umbrella guide on this area is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Destinations","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"Destinations"},"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/_Concurrency/AsyncSequence/batch(clock:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathers the records into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":" while any are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"}